d the problem of  basically um wanting to  [Music]  you know express simply  um evaluate the probability distribution  over all the paths a an electron say  could could could take  and he realized that that was a you know  an intractable  um integration problem he could you  couldn't work out the sort of  the normalization constant to make sure  that probability distribution  summoned to one so he was faced with an  intractable  um effectively integration problem in  quantum electrodynamics  so he solved him by converting that  integration problem into an optimization  problem  and the way he did it was to introduce a  variation free energy  that was always greater than the  quantity that he wanted to minimize or  was less than  the quantity that he wanted to maximize  which in this instance is just  the marginal likelihood or the  likelihood distribution of various paths  say a small particle might take um so  that's where i learned about free energy  essentially a thyme and if i'm an free  energy  that was provided a bound approximation  to something that you actually wanted to  maximize or optimize  and in my world that that thing you want  to  maximize is the model evidence or the  marginal likelihood  because back to self-evidencing but also  the marginal likelihood  sort of indicating that this is a  central notion in in physics  in bayesian statistics as as well  and that quantity that variation free  energy um has been in play now for  for for for you know not quite a century  but certainly many many decades  um currently known as an um an elbow  elbow and evidence lower bound  so that evidence lower bound underwrites  you know all of high-end machine  learning um  and you know certain simply reduced  cases of it i  i would i would actually suggest  probably all of machine learning at some  point um refer to or can be uh  seen as a special case of this the other  route  um inherits more from the russian side  um and this is you know your notions of  algorithmic complexity underlying  universal computation  via common growth complexity and sort of  induction  um so the big drive there  is is again formulating  universal computation as basically  communicating or articulating or  encoding  some structure in the simplest way  possible  by introducing a bound  on the thing that you want to you want  to  optimize or minimize or extremize so you  can also  find the free energy  in the context of um sort of  um a more shallow nest  like uh take on on communication and  optimization  and david mckay sort of originally  um brought that perspective to the table  perspective  that was was um well understood by  people like uh wallace in uh  melbourne who themselves had  taken it from from the the russian  literature and so on  i think he was he was an american but  also uh  you know taking his algorithmic  complexity so it's a very long answer to  to actually say that the free energy  principle  or the principle of minimizing free  energy  has underwritten um universal  computation  uh practical approaches to quantum  electrodynamics  and machine learning since since the  1950s  so it was you know that's what the free  energy means it's not the  the energy is costless it's it's it's  just  uh borrows from the formalism  of the thermodynamic uh free energy  either gibbs or a helmholtz  free energy  you

